A||||6||Deer_Slayer||question about tricolor fiero||||5||
Z||000000||Deer_Slayer||01-24-2000||01:48 PM||||While driving back and forth to school everyday, I've been seeing an 85 fiero coupe sitting in a NAPA store parking lot.  The car is black with silver on the bottom and a wide red stripe on top running from the trim on the front fascia to the rear decklid.  the car also has a spoiler and steel wheels with plastic hubcaps(probably now original).  Last week, I finally stoped by and asked the mechanic-owner about the car.  He said he planned on doing some work and eventually sell it.  I then looked at the car and took some pictures.  The interior and paint job looked to be in good shape, but the fascia emblem was missing and the paint underneith was black.  I thought about aquiring the car if the price was right, but I wonder if the paint was original.  I can't really afford to do an all out restoration.  I would appreciate any advice.   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-24-2000||08:29 PM||||The red stripe is the only thing that is not stock most likely. Fieros went 2 tone from 85 to 87 I beleive. Someone else would probably know all of the combos but black with silver was one of them.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Standard||01-25-2000||12:08 AM||||The red stripe is not original.  Any car with the ground effects (85 GT and 86-87 GT/SE) will be 2 tone.  So far as I know the only color the effects came in was silver.  88 GT's were monochromatic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||01-25-2000||05:59 AM||||Does anyone have or seen a 85GT with factory pin stripping above the side molding and on the wing? I have a black 85 with a red and white (two stripes) around the car. it appears to be factory painted (not vinyl) and under the clear coat. I have seen one other on the net witn identical stripping. Can anyone confirm that it,s factory?   ||||reg||5
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||03:46 PM||||There were some red 85 GTs with black striping on the bottom.<P>I could be wrong but pinstriping was not an option from the factory.||||reg||3
Z||000005||DRH||01-25-2000||04:12 PM||||Never heard of factory pinstripes either (although I could be wrong also  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Some cars have factory looking pinstripes done by the dealer. Usually part of some "package" that let's them increase their profit margin.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||01-26-2000||03:40 PM||||I worked at a volkswagon and Mazda dealership and they used to put on pin striping after the car got to the dealership.  Those rabbits needed spiffing up.  Some even got graphics and mags.  ||||reg||1
